  "answer": "Four of the five cases were confirmed: 0d4893f5 at 1.0x and +1.0 s (S16), 048b974e at 0.8x and 0 s (S2), 1bbe02fc at 0.6x and \u22122.0 s (S26), and 07981e6a at 1.2x and +0.5 s (S9). Every repeat at those settings failed. Their ranges still reach well below certainty because each rests on only three runs. None of these failures involves the pedestrian. In every failed run the policy drifted left or ignored a right-turn route. It then hit a parked car, an oncoming van or a car in the next lane, or it left the road. So speed and pedestrian timing are not what drives these failures. On 1bbe02fc and 07981e6a, every setting tried failed, including the nominal 1.0x / 0 s on 1bbe02fc. These cases fill top-k slots, but they do not show a dangerous speed\u2013timing combination. All of S2's failures are flagged as possible simulator artifacts (the ego ended up over 3.5 m off the recorded path), although the triage puts them on the policy.",
